Author: b <a@b>
Date:   Mon Oct 12 15:41:57 2026 -0700

    REFACTOR-0002: the core owns a BookingStore port, and JSON is one adapter
    
    The FileSystem interface from TEST-0001 was shaped like Node's fs:
    read a path, write a path. So anything that depended on it, including
    every test, had to know the path and the file's format. That's why
    FEAT-0001 changed every test.
    
    src/core/BookingStore.ts is the interface the core wants instead, in
    its own terms: the bookings on a date, and add a booking. The core
    declares it, so the core depends on nothing outside itself. Node's fs
    can't implement it, so JsonBookingStore adapts fs to it, the same way
    SpotifyAdapter adapted the Spotify SDK to MusicSource. The file's path
    and format version now live only in that adapter.
    
    BookingDesk is the core's use case: ask the store for the day's
    bookings, ask refusalFor(), and add the request if nothing refuses it.
    main.ts is left with the jobs at the edge: read argv, word the answer,
    and pick the real store. run() takes the store, so main.ts is the one
    place that names JsonBookingStore.
    
    The FakeBookingStore tests replace the FakeFileSystem ones. They hand
    over Booking objects, not JSON, so none of them knows the file format.

